{"title":"Rational function","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A rational function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is defined as any function that can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9c5380e90782dbea4dec2d13557a21d1a1d876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"41\" height=\"43\" /> for polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_function&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018044236\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.009 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 704/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.896      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.896      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15109:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018044236 and revision id 172398. Rendering was triggered because: page-vie